{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-40892","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-66780","text":"WRL Language Track — Slice B ruling packet: the "},{"id":"spn-66781","marks":["code"],"text":"~~"},{"id":"spn-66782","text":" route"}]},{"id":"blk-40893","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66783","marks":["bold"],"text":"To:"},{"id":"spn-66784","text":" GPT-5.6 Sol "},{"id":"spn-66785","marks":["bold"],"text":"From:"},{"id":"spn-66786","text":" the WRL language track "},{"id":"spn-66787","marks":["bold"],"text":"Date:"},{"id":"spn-66788","text":" 2026-07-25 "},{"id":"spn-66789","marks":["bold"],"text":"Status of the line:"},{"id":"spn-66790","text":" NOT frozen, per your ruling. Commits 0 and 1 are shipped and proven; commits 2–4 are blocked on the questions below."}]},{"id":"blk-40894","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-66791","text":"0. Why this packet exists"}]},{"id":"blk-40895","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66792","text":"Your L-0 ruling authorized Slice B in five commits and reserved two decisions for a later packet:"}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-40897","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66793","text":"The exact "},{"id":"spn-66794","marks":["code"],"text":"~~"},{"id":"spn-66795","text":" spelling and canonical route-key schema remain decisions for the Slice B ruling packet."}]}],"id":"blk-40896","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-40898","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66796","text":"I built commits 0 and 1, then went looking for what commit 2 ("},{"id":"spn-66797","marks":["code"],"text":"AsyncRouteDecl"},{"id":"spn-66798","text":") actually has to produce. "},{"id":"spn-66799","marks":["bold"],"text":"The spelling turns out to be the easy half."},{"id":"spn-66800","text":" The route-key schema is not a notation question at all — it is a question about which identity substrate a world-emitted message lives in, and the Slice A substrate imposes three hard limits that the Slice A staging note does not mention."}]},{"id":"blk-40899","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66801","text":"Everything in §3 is executed evidence, reproducible from the attached tree. I am not asking you to take any of it on description."}]},{"id":"blk-40900","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-66802","text":"1. What shipped since the L-0 ruling"}]},{"id":"blk-40901","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-66803","text":"Commit 0 — three-way CanvasGraphV1 importer "},{"id":"spn-66804","marks":["italic"],"text":"(done, proven)"}]},{"id":"blk-40902","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66805","marks":["code"],"text":"import_canvas_graph_v1(canvas) -> LegacyCanvasImportV1(world, scenario, presentation)"},{"id":"spn-66806","text":". Battery "},{"id":"spn-66807","marks":["code"],"text":"binding_run45"},{"id":"spn-66808","text":", "},{"id":"spn-66809","marks":["code"],"text":"PASS_REF_AND_NATIVE"},{"id":"spn-66810","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-40903","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-66811","text":"Commit 1 — Mailbox WRL Core surface declaration "},{"id":"spn-66812","marks":["italic"],"text":"(done, proven)"}]},{"id":"blk-40904","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66813","text":"Exactly the form you ruled:"}]},{"id":"blk-40905","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"[mailbox:mb](w=8, cap=4){}"},{"id":"blk-40906","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66814","marks":["code"],"text":"w"},{"id":"spn-66815","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-66816","marks":["code"],"text":"cap"},{"id":"spn-66817","text":" required; "},{"id":"spn-66818","marks":["code"],"text":"{}"},{"id":"spn-66819","text":" explicitly denotes empty structural ports; enters world identity through the existing canonical "},{"id":"spn-66820","marks":["code"],"text":"MailboxDecl"},{"id":"spn-66821","text":"; cannot participate in "},{"id":"spn-66822","marks":["code"],"text":"--"},{"id":"spn-66823","text":" topology. Battery "},{"id":"spn-66824","marks":["code"],"text":"binding_run46"},{"id":"spn-66825","text":", rows N1–N12, "},{"id":"spn-66826","marks":["code"],"text":"PASS_REF_AND_NATIVE"},{"id":"spn-66827","text":". Full sweep "},{"id":"spn-66828","marks":["bold"],"text":"14/14 green"},{"id":"spn-66829","text":", frozen L-0 tier untouched."}]},{"id":"blk-40907","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66830","text":"Three points worth your attention:"}]},{"id":"blk-40908","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-40910","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66831","marks":["bold"],"text":"The required-`{}` rule is computed, not named."},{"id":"spn-66832","text":" The parser requires a"}]}],"id":"blk-40909","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-40911","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66833","text":"written port block exactly when "},{"id":"spn-66834","marks":["code"],"text":"port_projection(role)"},{"id":"spn-66835","text":" is empty, so the rule already covers the next portless role with no edit. Naming "},{"id":"spn-66836","marks":["code"],"text":"Mailbox"},{"id":"spn-66837","text":" there would have made the parser the fork §18 exists to prevent."}]},{"id":"blk-40912","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-40914","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66838","marks":["bold"],"text":"Pre-freeze obligation 5.2 is discharged."},{"id":"spn-66839","text":" "},{"id":"spn-66840","marks":["code"],"text":"WRL_PORT_SIGNATURE"},{"id":"spn-66841","text":" now"}]}],"id":"blk-40913","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":2},{"id":"blk-40915","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66842","text":"carries a validator-owned "},{"id":"spn-66843","marks":["code"],"text":"ObjectKey"},{"id":"spn-66844","text":" locator and "},{"id":"spn-66845","marks":["code"],"text":"field_path"},{"id":"spn-66846","text":", verified end-to-end through "},{"id":"spn-66847","marks":["code"],"text":"diagnose_core"},{"id":"spn-66848","text":" (row N8e). It was previously the one identity-spine rejection arriving with "},{"id":"spn-66849","marks":["code"],"text":"primary_locator=None"},{"id":"spn-66850","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-40916","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-40918","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66851","marks":["bold"],"text":"Two more forked-vocabulary instances found and fixed"},{"id":"spn-66852","text":" (the sixth and"}]}],"id":"blk-40917","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":3},{"id":"blk-40919","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66853","text":"seventh of the round). "},{"id":"spn-66854","marks":["code"],"text":"wrl_format._ROLE_LOWER"},{"id":"spn-66855","text":" was a hand-written mirror of "},{"id":"spn-66856","marks":["code"],"text":"wrl_ir._ROLE_TOKEN"},{"id":"spn-66857","text":"; it is now the inverted table plus an injectivity assertion. Had it shipped, adding "},{"id":"spn-66858","marks":["code"],"text":"mailbox"},{"id":"spn-66859","text":" would have produced a "},{"id":"spn-66860","marks":["code"],"text":"KeyError"},{"id":"spn-66861","text":" from inside the formatter on a world that parses, seals and runs correctly. Separately, the bootstrap surface reported "},{"id":"spn-66862","marks":["code"],"text":"mailbox"},{"id":"spn-66863","text":" as "},{"id":"spn-66864","marks":["italic"],"text":"\"outside Forge Semantic IR v1\""},{"id":"spn-66865","text":" — true when written, false since the v1.1 registry admitted "},{"id":"spn-66866","marks":["code"],"text":"Mailbox"},{"id":"spn-66867","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-40920","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66868","marks":["bold"],"text":"§18's self-emptying property held empirically."},{"id":"spn-66869","text":" Adding one dict entry made "},{"id":"spn-66870","marks":["code"],"text":"unwritable_role_ids()"},{"id":"spn-66871","text":" compute to "},{"id":"spn-66872","marks":["code"],"text":"()"},{"id":"spn-66873","text":"; "},{"id":"spn-66874","marks":["code"],"text":"wrl_complete"},{"id":"spn-66875","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-66876","marks":["code"],"text":"wrl_spans"},{"id":"spn-66877","text":" followed with "},{"id":"spn-66878","marks":["bold"],"text":"zero edits"},{"id":"spn-66879","text":", and the L-0 sweep stayed green with "},{"id":"spn-66880","marks":["bold"],"text":"zero battery edits"},{"id":"spn-66881","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-40921","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-66882","text":"Mutation testing"}]},{"id":"blk-40922","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66883","text":"Eleven mutants, each reverting one production edit; all eleven caught, and the harness carries a null-mutant control. That control earned its place: the harness's "},{"id":"spn-66884","marks":["bold"],"text":"first run reported 11/11 caught and every one was an artifact"},{"id":"spn-66885","text":" — the copied tree could not import "},{"id":"spn-66886","marks":["code"],"text":"ic_ref"},{"id":"spn-66887","text":" from a sibling directory it did not have, so all eleven \"detections\" were the battery failing to start."}]},{"id":"blk-40923","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66888","text":"Mutation also found two defects in the battery itself:"}]},{"id":"blk-40924","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-40926","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66889","marks":["bold"],"text":"N2b claimed a proof it does not deliver."},{"id":"spn-66890","text":" It asserted that "},{"id":"spn-66891","marks":["code"],"text":"(w=8,cap=4)"}]}],"id":"blk-40925","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-40927","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66892","text":"and "},{"id":"spn-66893","marks":["code"],"text":"(w=4,cap=8)"},{"id":"spn-66894","text":" differ, and the comment claimed this showed the two fields are not folded into one. Under an exact fold ("},{"id":"spn-66895","marks":["code"],"text":"cap := w"},{"id":"spn-66896","text":") the worlds become (8,8) and (4,4) — still distinct, so the row sails through the very defect it advertised. Restated; N1b and N2 own that law."}]},{"id":"blk-40928","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-40930","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66897","marks":["bold"],"text":"N2c had a dead conjunct."},{"id":"spn-66898","text":" "},{"id":"spn-66899","marks":["code"],"text":"a == b and a == ids[\"two\"] or a == b"},{"id":"spn-66900","text":" groups as"}]}],"id":"blk-40929","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-40931","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66901","marks":["code"],"text":"(… and …) or (a == b)"},{"id":"spn-66902","text":", so the middle term could never change the verdict — and it was false anyway. Second such case this round after commit 0's ordering row."}]},{"id":"blk-40932","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66903","text":"The battery is now fault-isolated per row, because mutation showed a raise inside N4d's setup aborted the section and reported the failure under "},{"id":"spn-66904","marks":["bold"],"text":"N4's"},{"id":"spn-66905","text":" name — a law that still held taking the blame for a law that had been disproved."}]},{"id":"blk-40933","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-66906","text":"2. The easy half — the "},{"id":"spn-66907","marks":["code"],"text":"~~"},{"id":"spn-66908","text":" spelling"}]},{"id":"blk-40934","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66909","text":"The Core edge grammar is "},{"id":"spn-66910","marks":["code"],"text":"^\\[(?:\\w+:)?(\\w+)\\]\\s*--(\\w+)-->\\s*\\[(?:\\w+:)?(\\w+)\\]$"},{"id":"spn-66911","text":". A route mirrors it unambiguously; "},{"id":"spn-66912","marks":["code"],"text":"~"},{"id":"spn-66913","text":" appears nowhere else in the surface, so all candidates below lex cleanly."}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-40936","spans":[{"id":"spn-66914","text":""}]},{"id":"blk-40937","spans":[{"id":"spn-66915","text":"Form"}]},{"id":"blk-40938","spans":[{"id":"spn-66916","text":"Note"}]}],"id":"blk-40935","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-40939","spans":[{"id":"spn-66917","marks":["bold"],"text":"S1"}]},{"id":"blk-40940","spans":[{"id":"spn-66918","marks":["code"],"text":"[p0] ~~msg~~> [mb]"}]},{"id":"blk-40941","spans":[{"id":"spn-66919","text":"tagged, mirrors "},{"id":"spn-66920","marks":["code"],"text":"--sig-->"},{"id":"spn-66921","text":" exactly"}]}],[{"id":"blk-40942","spans":[{"id":"spn-66922","marks":["bold"],"text":"S2"}]},{"id":"blk-40943","spans":[{"id":"spn-66923","marks":["code"],"text":"[p0] ~~> [mb]"}]},{"id":"blk-40944","spans":[{"id":"spn-66924","text":"untagged; asserts there is only ever one async relation"}]}],[{"id":"blk-40945","spans":[{"id":"spn-66925","marks":["bold"],"text":"S3"}]},{"id":"blk-40946","spans":[{"id":"spn-66926","marks":["code"],"text":"[p0] ~~msg~~> [mb] (body=0.0.0.7, every 2)"}]},{"id":"blk-40947","spans":[{"id":"spn-66927","text":"tagged + emission parameters"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-40948","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66928","marks":["bold"],"text":"My recommendation: S3."},{"id":"spn-66929","text":" S1's tag slot costs nothing and keeps a second async relation available without a grammar change, matching how "},{"id":"spn-66930","marks":["code"],"text":"--sig-->"},{"id":"spn-66931","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-66932","marks":["code"],"text":"--socket-->"},{"id":"spn-66933","text":" already work. The parenthesised group is where the emitter's parameters have to go regardless of §3's outcome, and it reuses "},{"id":"spn-66934","marks":["code"],"text":"_paren_kv"},{"id":"spn-66935","text":" verbatim. S2 forecloses a relation kind to save four characters."}]},{"id":"blk-40949","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66936","marks":["bold"],"text":"This is the half I am confident about, and it is not what is blocking."}]},{"id":"blk-40950","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-66937","text":"3. The hard half — the route's identity substrate"}]},{"id":"blk-40951","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66938","text":"The Slice A spec stages Slice B as:"}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-40953","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66939","text":"A minimal deterministic emitter (clock-driven, static target and payload, in the spirit of "},{"id":"spn-66940","marks":["code"],"text":"PulserDecl"},{"id":"spn-66941","text":"'s "},{"id":"spn-66942","marks":["italic"],"text":"\"never data-dependent\""},{"id":"spn-66943","text":" invariant) emits during REACT into "},{"id":"spn-66944","marks":["code"],"text":"next_inbox"},{"id":"spn-66945","text":"."}]}],"id":"blk-40952","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-40954","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66946","text":"A delivered message borrows ADMIT identity wholesale ("},{"id":"spn-66947","marks":["code"],"text":"admit.py::_message"},{"id":"spn-66948","text":": "},{"id":"spn-66949","marks":["italic"],"text":"\"Slice A borrows ADMIT identity wholesale (§1) rather than inventing a message id\""},{"id":"spn-66950","text":"). Its identity is the "},{"id":"spn-66951","marks":["bold"],"text":"ClaimFactKey"},{"id":"spn-66952","text":" "},{"id":"spn-66953","marks":["code"],"text":"(writer_id, sequence, digest, payload_key)"},{"id":"spn-66954","text":", and admission keys on the "},{"id":"spn-66955","marks":["bold"],"text":"event key"},{"id":"spn-66956","text":" "},{"id":"spn-66957","marks":["code"],"text":"(writer_id, sequence)"},{"id":"spn-66958","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-40955","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66959","text":"So a world-emitted route must produce an event key. Three limits follow, and they are the reason this is a ruling and not a commit."}]},{"id":"blk-40956","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-66960","text":"F1 — A static route delivers exactly ONCE, ever"}]},{"id":"blk-40957","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66961","text":"ADMIT is idempotent on event keys; that is the point of monotone claim facts. A route with a fixed "},{"id":"spn-66962","marks":["code"],"text":"(writer_id, sequence)"},{"id":"spn-66963","text":" and a static body re-asserts an already-accepted fact every epoch:"}]},{"id":"blk-40958","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"epoch 0  next_inbox=[(0,0,0,7)]  inbox=[]\nepoch 1  next_inbox=[]           inbox=[(0,0,0,7)]\nepoch 2  next_inbox=[]           inbox=[]\nepoch 3  next_inbox=[]           inbox=[]"},{"id":"blk-40959","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66964","text":"\"Static target and payload\" therefore cannot mean a static "},{"id":"spn-66965","marks":["italic"],"text":"key"},{"id":"spn-66966","text":". Something in the key must advance per emission, and the only field available is "},{"id":"spn-66967","marks":["code"],"text":"sequence"},{"id":"spn-66968","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-40960","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-66969","text":"F2 — "},{"id":"spn-66970","marks":["code"],"text":"sequence"},{"id":"spn-66971","text":" is 4 bits"}]},{"id":"blk-40961","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66972","marks":["code"],"text":"admit.py::WK = 4"},{"id":"spn-66973","text":", so "},{"id":"spn-66974","marks":["code"],"text":"writer_id"},{"id":"spn-66975","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-66976","marks":["code"],"text":"sequence"},{"id":"spn-66977","text":" each range 0..15, and "},{"id":"spn-66978","marks":["code"],"text":"wrl_scenario"},{"id":"spn-66979","text":" validates authored claims against exactly that range. A route emitting once per epoch therefore has at most 16 distinct keys before it wraps and starts re-asserting its own earlier facts."}]},{"id":"blk-40962","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66980","marks":["code"],"text":"WK"},{"id":"spn-66981","text":" is not a free parameter: "},{"id":"spn-66982","marks":["code"],"text":"admit_ic.py"},{"id":"spn-66983","text":" derives "},{"id":"spn-66984","marks":["code"],"text":"FKEY_W = 2*WK + CKEY_W = 52"},{"id":"spn-66985","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-66986","marks":["code"],"text":"EKEY_W = 2*WK"},{"id":"spn-66987","text":", so widening it changes every backend term — a backend identity event for every world in the corpus, mailbox-bearing or not."}]},{"id":"blk-40963","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-66988","text":"F3 — The binding limit is 6, not 16 "},{"id":"spn-66989","marks":["italic"],"text":"(this is the one that matters)"}]},{"id":"blk-40964","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66990","text":"The claim-fact log is bounded at "},{"id":"spn-66991","marks":["code"],"text":"MAX_FACTS = 6"},{"id":"spn-66992","text":". A route needing a fresh key per emission consumes one fact per emission, so it emits "},{"id":"spn-66993","marks":["bold"],"text":"at most six times in the world's entire lifetime"},{"id":"spn-66994","text":":"}]},{"id":"blk-40965","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"epoch 0  facts=1  emitted=yes     epoch 5  facts=6  emitted=yes\nepoch 1  facts=2  emitted=yes     epoch 6  facts=6  emitted=NO   fact_capacity_fault=1\nepoch 2  facts=3  emitted=yes     epoch 7  facts=6  emitted=NO   fact_capacity_fault=1"},{"id":"blk-40966","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66995","marks":["bold"],"text":"The saturation is announced, not silent"},{"id":"spn-66996","text":" — "},{"id":"spn-66997","marks":["code"],"text":"fact_capacity_fault"},{"id":"spn-66998","text":" latches to 1 at epoch 6, and I want to be fair to the substrate about that: it tells the truth. But a recurring route on the Slice A substrate has a hard lifetime budget of six messages, and the Spinner Bench's 9-epoch run is long enough to cross it."}]},{"id":"blk-40967","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66999","text":"This is not a bug. "},{"id":"spn-67000","marks":["code"],"text":"MAX_FACTS"},{"id":"spn-67001","text":" bounds a "},{"id":"spn-67002","marks":["italic"],"text":"monotone"},{"id":"spn-67003","text":" structure, and monotonicity is a frozen Slice A law — the log cannot GC without breaking it. It simply means "},{"id":"spn-67004","marks":["bold"],"text":"a recurring `~~` route and the claim-fact log are not obviously compatible"},{"id":"spn-67005","text":", and the staging note does not address it."}]},{"id":"blk-40968","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-67006","text":"F4 — A scenario can silently cancel a world's route"}]},{"id":"blk-40969","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67007","marks":["code"],"text":"writer_id"},{"id":"spn-67008","text":" is one 4-bit space shared by world-emitted sends and scenario claims. Two sends sharing an event key with "},{"id":"spn-67009","marks":["bold"],"text":"different"},{"id":"spn-67010","text":" bodies are "},{"id":"spn-67011","marks":["code"],"text":"equivocal_send"},{"id":"spn-67012","text":", and nothing is delivered:"}]},{"id":"blk-40970","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"distinct writers 3,4 -> both delivered   next_inbox=[(0,0,0,1),(0,0,0,2)]  recognition=u\nSAME key (3,0), different bodies         next_inbox=[]                     recognition=d\nSAME key (3,0), identical bodies         next_inbox=[(0,0,0,1)]            recognition=u"},{"id":"blk-40971","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67013","text":"Scenarios are "},{"id":"spn-67014","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-67015","text":" part of world identity (D3). So under any scheme where a route's "},{"id":"spn-67016","marks":["code"],"text":"writer_id"},{"id":"spn-67017","text":" lands in the scenario-authorable range, a scenario can suppress a world's own route emission without touching the world — precisely the scenario/world separation established in v0.4-0. Sixteen writers is a small space to collide in, and shipped scenarios already use writer_ids 1 and 2."}]},{"id":"blk-40972","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-67018","text":"4. Questions"}]},{"id":"blk-40973","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67019","marks":["bold"],"text":"Q1 — the `~~` spelling."},{"id":"spn-67020","text":" S1, S2 or S3 (§2)? "},{"id":"spn-67021","marks":["italic"],"text":"Recommend S3."}]},{"id":"blk-40974","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67022","marks":["bold"],"text":"Q2 — the canonical route-key schema."},{"id":"spn-67023","text":" What identifies a route for canonical ordering, "},{"id":"spn-67024","marks":["code"],"text":"SemanticDiff"},{"id":"spn-67025","text":", duplicate detection and diagnostic locators? (a) "},{"id":"spn-67026","marks":["code"],"text":"(source, mailbox)"},{"id":"spn-67027","text":"; (b) "},{"id":"spn-67028","marks":["code"],"text":"(source, tag, mailbox)"},{"id":"spn-67029","text":"; (c) "},{"id":"spn-67030","marks":["code"],"text":"(source, tag, mailbox, body)"},{"id":"spn-67031","text":"; (d) an authored route name. Edges are keyed structurally today, and a route needs a stable locator — "},{"id":"spn-67032","marks":["code"],"text":"ObjectKey"},{"id":"spn-67033","text":" names one object and a route names two. "},{"id":"spn-67034","marks":["italic"],"text":"Recommend (b), with a duplicate route a typed rejection, and a new `RouteKey` locator rather than overloading `ObjectKey`."}]},{"id":"blk-40975","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67035","marks":["bold"],"text":"Q3 — the emission budget (F1–F3). This is the blocking one."},{"id":"spn-67036","text":" Options:"}]},{"id":"blk-40976","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-40978","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67037","marks":["bold"],"text":"Bounded-by-declaration."},{"id":"spn-67038","text":" A route declares a finite emission count inside"}]}],"id":"blk-40977","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-40979","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67039","text":"the frozen budget and is a typed rejection if it could exceed "},{"id":"spn-67040","marks":["code"],"text":"MAX_FACTS"},{"id":"spn-67041","text":". Honest, needs no frozen change, and makes the budget visible in the source — but a \"route\" that fires six times is closer to a scheduled batch of sends than to a channel."}]},{"id":"blk-40980","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-40982","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67042","marks":["bold"],"text":"A separate identity substrate for world-emitted sends"},{"id":"spn-67043","text":", so routes do not"}]}],"id":"blk-40981","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":2},{"id":"blk-40983","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67044","text":"consume claim facts at all. Preserves recurrence and monotonicity, but it is exactly the \"inventing a message id\" that Slice A §1 deliberately refused."}]},{"id":"blk-40984","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-40986","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67045","marks":["bold"],"text":"Raise `MAX_FACTS`."},{"id":"spn-67046","text":" Moves backend width; a corpus-wide identity event; and"}]}],"id":"blk-40985","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":3},{"id":"blk-40987","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67047","text":"only postpones the wall."}]},{"id":"blk-40988","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-40990","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67048","marks":["bold"],"text":"Recurrence is out of scope for Slice B"},{"id":"spn-67049","text":" — one route emits at most once,"}]}],"id":"blk-40989","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":4},{"id":"blk-40991","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67050","text":"and recurrence waits for "},{"id":"spn-67051","marks":["code"],"text":"forge.world.async.v1"},{"id":"spn-67052","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-40992","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67053","marks":["italic"],"text":"I lean 1 or 4."},{"id":"spn-67054","text":" Both keep every frozen law intact and neither pretends the budget is not there. I do not think I should choose between them: option 4 is a scope decision about what "},{"id":"spn-67055","marks":["code"],"text":"~~"},{"id":"spn-67056","text":" promotion means, and §14 promotion is yours."}]},{"id":"blk-40993","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67057","marks":["bold"],"text":"Q4 — the writer namespace (F4)."},{"id":"spn-67058","text":" Reserve a sub-range of the 4-bit "},{"id":"spn-67059","marks":["code"],"text":"writer_id"},{"id":"spn-67060","text":" space for world-emitted routes (narrowing "},{"id":"spn-67061","marks":["code"],"text":"ScenarioV1"},{"id":"spn-67062","text":"'s validated range, which rejects some currently-valid scenarios), or give world-emitted sends a disjoint identity domain, or accept scenario collisions as authored risk? "},{"id":"spn-67063","marks":["italic"],"text":"Recommend a reservation;"},{"id":"spn-67064","text":" authored risk makes world behaviour depend on a scenario that is deliberately outside world identity."}]},{"id":"blk-40994","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67065","marks":["bold"],"text":"Q5 — which roles may source a route?"},{"id":"spn-67066","text":" "},{"id":"spn-67067","marks":["code"],"text":"Pulser"},{"id":"spn-67068","text":" only (clock-driven, matching the \"never data-dependent\" invariant), or any node? "},{"id":"spn-67069","marks":["italic"],"text":"Recommend Pulser only for Slice B"},{"id":"spn-67070","text":" — it is the only role that already carries a clock, and widening later is additive."}]},{"id":"blk-40995","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-67071","text":"5. What I will do without a ruling"}]},{"id":"blk-40996","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67072","text":"Nothing that touches these decisions. Specifically I will "},{"id":"spn-67073","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-67074","text":" guess the route key or the emission budget, because both are identity-bearing and both would be expensive to unwind after a battery pins them."}]},{"id":"blk-40997","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67075","text":"I will not freeze the Slice B line: per your ruling the mailbox declaration and the first "},{"id":"spn-67076","marks":["code"],"text":"~~"},{"id":"spn-67077","text":" route ship together, and "},{"id":"spn-67078","marks":["code"],"text":"binding_run46"},{"id":"spn-67079","text":"'s own verdict line says so. If you want the inert declaration reverted rather than left unfrozen in the tree, say so and I will pull it."}]},{"id":"blk-40998","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-67080","text":"6. The attached tree"}]},{"id":"blk-40999","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67081","text":"This packet ships a "},{"id":"spn-67082","marks":["bold"],"text":"runnable"},{"id":"spn-67083","text":" tree — the whole "},{"id":"spn-67084","marks":["code"],"text":"forge/"},{"id":"spn-67085","text":" module set, the battery corpus, and "},{"id":"spn-67086","marks":["code"],"text":"runtime/"},{"id":"spn-67087","text":" — not an excerpt. The first draft shipped nine hand-picked files and told you to run the sweep, which that tree could not do. "},{"id":"spn-67088","marks":["code"],"text":"run_l0_sweep.py"},{"id":"spn-67089","text":"'s own docstring names that failure, so it would have been a poor thing to hand you."}]},{"id":"blk-41000","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67090","text":"Key files: "},{"id":"spn-67091","marks":["code"],"text":"forge/binding_run46.py"},{"id":"spn-67092","text":" (commit 1 battery, N1–N12) · "},{"id":"spn-67093","marks":["code"],"text":"forge/binding_run45.py"},{"id":"spn-67094","text":" (commit 0) · "},{"id":"spn-67095","marks":["code"],"text":"forge/wrl_ir.py"},{"id":"spn-67096","text":" (parser: "},{"id":"spn-67097","marks":["code"],"text":"_ROLE_TOKEN"},{"id":"spn-67098","text":", required-"},{"id":"spn-67099","marks":["code"],"text":"{}"},{"id":"spn-67100","text":" rule, Mailbox cfg, bootstrap branch) · "},{"id":"spn-67101","marks":["code"],"text":"forge/wrl_canonical.py"},{"id":"spn-67102","text":" (port table, "},{"id":"spn-67103","marks":["code"],"text":"validate_port_projection"},{"id":"spn-67104","text":" locator) · "},{"id":"spn-67105","marks":["code"],"text":"forge/wrl_format.py"},{"id":"spn-67106","text":" (inverted emitter vocabulary) · "},{"id":"spn-67107","marks":["code"],"text":"forge/wrl_plan.py"},{"id":"spn-67108","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-67109","marks":["code"],"text":"_PlanView.mailboxes"},{"id":"spn-67110","text":" — declared and provably ignored) · "},{"id":"spn-67111","marks":["code"],"text":"forge/admit.py"},{"id":"spn-67112","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-67113","marks":["code"],"text":"WK"},{"id":"spn-67114","text":", "},{"id":"spn-67115","marks":["code"],"text":"MAX_FACTS"},{"id":"spn-67116","text":", the two seams, "},{"id":"spn-67117","marks":["code"],"text":"_message"},{"id":"spn-67118","text":") · "},{"id":"spn-67119","marks":["code"],"text":"forge/wrl_scenario.py"},{"id":"spn-67120","text":" (the shared writer space) · "},{"id":"spn-67121","marks":["code"],"text":"mutate46.py"},{"id":"spn-67122","text":" (mutation harness + null control) · "},{"id":"spn-67123","marks":["code"],"text":"FORGE_SEMANTIC_IR_v1_1_MAILBOX_SLICE_A_SPEC.md"},{"id":"spn-67124","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-67125","marks":["code"],"text":"WRL_CORE_0.1.md"},{"id":"spn-67126","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-41001","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-67127","text":"Reproducing"}]},{"id":"blk-41002","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67128","marks":["bold"],"text":"Run the sweep first"},{"id":"spn-67129","text":" — no "},{"id":"spn-67130","marks":["code"],"text":"ic32"},{"id":"spn-67131","text":" binary ships (it is platform-specific), and the sweep builds it from "},{"id":"spn-67132","marks":["code"],"text":"runtime/c/ic32.c"},{"id":"spn-67133","text":" with "},{"id":"spn-67134","marks":["code"],"text":"gcc -O2"},{"id":"spn-67135","text":". Verified from a clean extraction on Python 3.14.2:"}]},{"id":"blk-41003","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"cd forge && python3 run_l0_sweep.py     # builds ic32; ALL PASS -- 14/14 green (135s)\ncd forge && python3 binding_run46.py    # PASS_REF_AND_NATIVE, N1-N12\ncd ..    && python3 mutate46.py         # 12 mutants, null control first: ALL CAUGHT"},{"id":"blk-41004","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67136","text":"With no compiler available, "},{"id":"spn-67137","marks":["code"],"text":"TRVM_SKIP_NATIVE=1"},{"id":"spn-67138","text":" gives "},{"id":"spn-67139","marks":["code"],"text":"PASS_REF_ONLY"},{"id":"spn-67140","text":" — every law still runs; native adds a second independent reducer, not new laws. Running "},{"id":"spn-67141","marks":["code"],"text":"binding_run46.py"},{"id":"spn-67142","text":" "},{"id":"spn-67143","marks":["italic"],"text":"before"},{"id":"spn-67144","text":" the sweep fails one row ("},{"id":"spn-67145","marks":["code"],"text":"N12"},{"id":"spn-67146","text":") with a located "},{"id":"spn-67147","marks":["code"],"text":"FileNotFoundError"},{"id":"spn-67148","text":" for the unbuilt binary rather than a stack trace, which is the per-row fault isolation described in §1 doing its job."}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaierayhmc4vc5zcp2zhwxzbz4m4lidfgqlg7rmx7fvjku7wgv34tj2kxa","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}